sblim-sfcc
------------------------------------------
SFCC is a CIM client for C that can directly access SFCB. You can use SFCC to
CIM-enable your programs. It will work with any CIMOM that supports CIM-XML;
however, SFCB can take advantage of the LocalConnect interface for improved
performance (no XML encoding/decoding overhead).

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libcimcclient0-2.2.8-1bl1
  libcurl4-8.23.0-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libcurl-devel-8.23.0-1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://sourceforge.net/projects/sblim/

Canonical download:
  mirror://sourceforge/sblim/sblim-sfcc-2.2.8.tar.bz2

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack sblim-sfcc-2.2.8-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./sblim-sfcc-2.2.8-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/sblim-sfcc-2.2.8-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/sblim-sfcc-2.2.8-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libcimcclient0-2.2.8-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libcimcclient-devel-2.2.8-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

